[00:00.83] (Raise your can of beer on high)
[00:05.78] (And seal your fate forever)
[00:11.11] (Our best years have past us by)
[00:16.54] (The golden age of leather)
[00:37.22] This was the night, not long to come
[00:39.91] In the year of our Lord A.D.
[00:43.56] Where in a desert way-house
[00:46.26] Poised on the brink of eternity
[00:50.75] Four and ninety studded horsemen closed the knot of honor
[00:57.01] As only drunken soldiers can
[01:03.37] And passed from man to man
[01:06.92] A wanton child, too dead to care
[01:09.69] That each would find his pleasure as he might
[01:16.03] For this fantastic night was billed
[01:20.52] As nothing less than the end of an age
[01:24.17] A last crusade, a final outrage
[01:27.79] In this day of flaccid plumage
[01:31.30] And there was worn no cloth but leather
[01:36.71] Made supple by years of stinging cinders
[01:43.02] And here were seen the scars of age
[01:48.42] For age had been the common call for one last night together
[02:32.50] (Dawn colored the sky) the ritual ceased
[02:43.40] (Some had died) they were buried with their bikes
[02:55.16] (Each grabbed a rag) from a man with a sack
[03:06.86] (Torn strips of color) the red and the black
[03:31.14] I came here willingly
[03:42.81] And I will go down valiantly
[03:53.67] (We made a vow) to give it all we had to give
[03:59.01] (We made a vow) to die as we had lived
[04:18.02] They flew the colors, they began to fight
[04:20.74] They flailed at each other like bugs at a light
[04:23.35] Bodies and bikes beyond repair
[04:26.11] The smell of oil and gas in the air
[04:35.15] Then the wind whipped the desert with a giant hand
[04:37.88] And the humans and the Harleys caught the shifting sand
[04:46.83] The old ranger weathered the storm
[04:49.56] And he topped the rise by the middle of morn
[04:52.26] He saw rippled dunes, calm and surreal
[04:56.80] And a glint of a solitary shaft of chromium steel
